---
title: Authoring dungeons
pageSlug: authoring-dungeons
mod: epicquest-dungeoning
section: config
order: 3
---

Build pieces in a creative world. Structure Block **SAVE** with a name that is not `minecraft:...`. `mypack:hall_1` will mirror into the pack folder.

```
config/epicquest_dungeoning/
  dungeons.json
  images/          optional key / GUI preview PNGs
  dungeons/<dungeon_id>/
    structures/<namespace>/.../*.nbt
    worldgen/template_pool/<namespace>/*.json
```

`dungeons.json` needs a `jigsaw` block: start pool, start jigsaw name, size, max distance, fallback pool, optional unique templates. Put a **Dungeon Player Spawn** in the start piece. Put a **Dungeon End Pad** only if completion is `reach_end`.

Keep a tiny dead-end in `fallback_pool`. Leftover connectors get stuffed with it. If you skip this, you get holes.

Uniques (boss room, treasure vault) belong in `unique_templates` with a depth band. Generates that never reach that band are thrown away and tried again. That is why you do not ship a “boss only” stub as the whole run.

**Dungeon Event Markers** go in the pieces. Creative, right-click, set `event_id` and `block_replace` (air is fine). Then ship:

```
data/<namespace>/dungeon_event/<path>.json
data/<namespace>/event_poll/<path>.json
```

The poll is a weighted command set. Commands run as the player. `~` is the marker. Each placed marker fires once until wipe or `/dungeon event reset`. Shared ids can chain with `chain_proximity`.

Completion: `kill_entity`, `collect_items`, `reach_end`, or omit it and extract with the button / API / `/dungeon complete`.

A first dungeon: three halls, one dead-end, one boss unique, start spawn, one event marker that opens a fence. `size` 8. If the boss never shows, raise size or loosen the depth ratios before you add more art.
